NVIDIA proprietary graphics driver 580.159.04 (R580 driver branch) for the
Gaming Live CD. Ships the full userspace stack (OpenGL, Vulkan ICD, OpenCL
ICD, CUDA, NVENC/NVDEC, GSP firmware) in both 64-bit and 32-bit form, plus
kernel modules built against the Linux 7.1.5 kernel that ships on the CD.

Install notes:
- The kernel modules are compiled during the recipe build against
  /System/Kernel/Modules/Current/build, so the Linux package must be
  installed on the build system first.
- nouveau is blacklisted and nvidia-drm modeset is enabled via
  /etc/modprobe.d/nvidia.conf.
- An Xorg Device section using the nvidia driver is installed via
  /etc/X11/xorg.conf.d/10-nvidia.conf.
- A udev rule manages /dev/nvidia* permissions.
- Vulkan apps get the NVIDIA ICD automatically via the Vulkan-Loader.
